      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To frame this as a threat rather than simple change, you can argue that deep cultural practices require time and continuity to thrive in a specific environment. Point out that rapid shifts disrupt the slow, organic way traditions are learned and passed down through generations. You can then assert that a sudden turnover risks eroding the very social fabric—the shared understanding of 'home'—that these traditions sustain. This allows the audience to see cultural maintenance as essential for social stability.",
